---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy — Buzzyfly"
	description="How Buzzyfly collects, uses, and stores information when you buy a product or join the email list."
	pubDate={new Date('September 16 2026')}
>
	<p>Last updated: November 4, 2026</p>

	<p>
		Buzzyfly (buzzyfly.com) sells a web app and digital templates for running a client business. This page explains what we collect, why, and how to reach us. Contact: support@buzzyfly.com.
	</p>

	<h2>What we collect</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Email address when you join the list or check out through Stripe or PayPal.</li>
		<li>Name and payment details handled by Stripe or PayPal. We never see or store your full card number.</li>
		<li>Order records needed to send your access link and handle refunds.</li>
		<li>Basic site analytics and security logs from our host (Cloudflare).</li>
		<li>Not your app data. The clients, notes and emails you enter in the web app are saved in your own browser. They are not sent to us.</li>
		<li>Where your visit came from: the campaign tag on the link (for example "reddit") or, if there is none, the name of the site that linked to us (for example "google.com"). It is kept in your browser for 30 days and saved with your signup or order, and counted in daily page-view totals, so we know which posts and ads work.</li>
		<li>Questions you type into the help chat on /support. They are sent to an AI service to write the answer (Cloudflare Workers AI, or another AI provider if that one is unavailable). Don't type payment details or private client information there.</li>
		<li>Emails you send to support@buzzyfly.com, and the IP address used when an access or download link is opened, to help stop shared or stolen links.</li>
		<li>If you join Buzzyfly Jobs, your email and membership status from Stripe, and a sign-in cookie that keeps the job listings unlocked on your device.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How we use it</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Give you access to what you paid for.</li>
		<li>Send the free weekly-reset checklist if you opted in.</li>
		<li>Send occasional product email if you are on the list. You can unsubscribe on any email.</li>
		<li>Answer support and process refunds.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Who else sees it</h2>
	<p>
		Stripe and PayPal process payments. Cloudflare hosts the site, stores order records and runs the help chat's AI. If Cloudflare's AI is unavailable, help chat questions may go to another AI provider (Groq, Google or xAI) to write the answer. Email is sent through our email provider when delivery and list emails go out. We do not sell your email or order data.
	</p>

	<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
	<p>
		Order records are kept as long as needed for delivery, refunds, tax, and fraud checks. List emails stay until you unsubscribe or ask to be deleted.
	</p>

	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<p>
		Email support@buzzyfly.com to get a copy of what we have, correct it, or delete list and account data we control. Stripe and PayPal hold payment records under their own policies.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies</h2>
	<p>
		The site uses cookies and similar tech for security, checkout, and basic analytics. You can block cookies in your browser; checkout may then fail.
	</p>
</Layout>
